WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.129
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.399 --> 00:45.608
Listen.

3
00:45.692 --> 00:48.570
You don't throw shuriken. You shoot them.

4
00:50.196 --> 00:51.197
Now!

5
00:53.950 --> 00:55.368
Well…

6
00:56.035 --> 00:58.830
everyone's suited to different things.

7
01:06.004 --> 01:07.755
Let's get the situation straight.

8
01:10.175 --> 01:14.262
After leaving Sunpu Castle, Ieyasu has entered Nijo Castle in Kyoto.

9
01:14.345 --> 01:17.974
His goal is clear: destroy Osaka Castle,

10
01:18.057 --> 01:20.351
crush the Toyotomi, and unite the realm.

11
01:20.435 --> 01:21.728
What about Hidetada's army?

12
01:21.811 --> 01:23.438
They've already left Edo.

13
01:23.521 --> 01:24.981
When will they join up?

14
01:25.064 --> 01:26.149
In about eight days.

15
01:26.232 --> 01:29.861
If we launch a surprise attack on Kyoto before their forces assemble,

16
01:29.944 --> 01:31.237
we might win.

17
01:31.321 --> 01:33.114
That's Lord Yukimura's plan.

18
01:33.197 --> 01:34.991
And Lady Yodo rejected it.

19
01:35.658 --> 01:38.494
Lady Yodo is the castle's de facto ruler.

20
01:39.412 --> 01:40.788
We can't defy her.

21
01:41.372 --> 01:45.043
But a siege puts us at a disadvantage, doesn't it?

22
01:45.126 --> 01:46.920
Not necessarily.

23
01:47.795 --> 01:49.547
If we can expect reinforcements,

24
01:49.631 --> 01:52.675
we can hold out until they arrive and trap the enemy in a pincer attack.

25
01:53.176 --> 01:55.970
We should assume no daimyo will side with the Toyotomi.

26
01:56.512 --> 01:58.306
It would be suicide.

27
02:00.225 --> 02:03.061
The gap between ideal and reality…

28
02:03.144 --> 02:06.773
Why aren't we allowed to attend the war council in the first place?

29
02:07.273 --> 02:13.529
Everyone in this castle looks down on us as scum with no loyalty.

30
02:14.197 --> 02:19.244
Must a ninja endure such treatment?

31
02:19.869 --> 02:25.041
Then why not use Saizo's transformation technique to impersonate Lady Yodo?

32
02:25.124 --> 02:27.961
We could tie up the real Lady Yodo somewhere…

33
02:28.044 --> 02:30.296
We'd all be beheaded if we did that.

34
02:30.380 --> 02:33.925
Besides, Saizo can't imitate a woman's mannerisms.

35
02:35.593 --> 02:37.470
You don't know women, huh?

36
02:37.553 --> 02:38.638
Shut up, you stupid monkey!

37
02:38.721 --> 02:40.265
What's that supposed to mean?

38
02:40.348 --> 02:41.474
Don't make things up!

39
02:41.557 --> 02:44.352
-It's because you… -Both of you, enough!

40
02:44.435 --> 02:45.979
Then I'll transform into her.

41
02:46.062 --> 02:47.480
As if a fool like you could.

42
02:48.064 --> 02:49.857
Yes I can!

43
02:50.608 --> 02:51.442
Hey!

44
02:54.112 --> 02:55.321
Excuse me.

45
03:01.828 --> 03:05.039
Lord Yukimura, Lady Yodo requests your presence.

46
03:05.123 --> 03:06.082
I'll be right there.

47
03:09.460 --> 03:10.920
I'm counting on you, old man.

48
03:11.671 --> 03:12.505
Sure.

49
03:14.549 --> 03:16.342
Come on, you go, too.

50
03:17.176 --> 03:19.345
-What? -We're gathering intel.

51
03:19.887 --> 03:21.806
You want to get strong like a ninja, right?

52
03:22.640 --> 03:23.474
Yes!

53
03:28.813 --> 03:29.981
I've brought him, my lady.

54
03:42.285 --> 03:45.705
I, Sanada Yukimura, have arrived.

55
03:46.497 --> 03:47.373
Well?

56
03:47.915 --> 03:50.043
How does it feel to be back after 20 years?

57
03:54.047 --> 03:56.799
It brings back many memories.

58
03:58.468 --> 03:59.635
Is that all?

59
04:17.278 --> 04:20.740
At the war council earlier, I spoke harshly to you.

60
04:21.741 --> 04:23.117
You must have taken offense.

61
04:24.869 --> 04:25.995
Not at all.

62
04:26.496 --> 04:28.414
Don't speak so formally.

63
04:29.999 --> 04:31.751
Hold me tight…

64
04:33.044 --> 04:34.337
like you used to…

65
04:37.215 --> 04:38.132
Lady Yodo.

66
04:39.050 --> 04:39.967
I beseech you

67
04:40.676 --> 04:42.678
to reconsider.

68
04:44.347 --> 04:46.224
With our provisions limited,

69
04:47.725 --> 04:48.810
a siege would…

70
04:48.893 --> 04:51.020
We've settled that matter already.

71
04:53.189 --> 04:54.232
All I ask

72
04:55.316 --> 04:58.277
is that you protect Hideyori.

73
05:01.697 --> 05:03.783
He's grown, hasn't he?

74
05:05.451 --> 05:06.619
His looks…

75
05:09.205 --> 05:12.291
and courage may not quite match yours, though.

76
05:14.585 --> 05:15.503
So he is…

77
05:22.802 --> 05:23.803
Lord Hideyori is…

78
05:25.930 --> 05:27.181
He's your son.

79
05:36.107 --> 05:39.694
Would you risk Hideyori's life by sending him into battle?

80
05:40.403 --> 05:42.405
You expect me to accept that as his mother?

81
05:45.616 --> 05:48.077
Never again speak of a plan

82
05:49.287 --> 05:50.913
that would put my son in danger.

83
06:22.320 --> 06:24.238
SOBA

84
06:24.322 --> 06:26.157
It'd be nice to open a shop like this.

85
06:26.240 --> 06:27.408
Yeah.

86
06:28.534 --> 06:30.036
You could open an apothecary.

87
06:30.703 --> 06:31.704
And I could open…

88
06:33.247 --> 06:34.248
a restaurant?

89
06:34.332 --> 06:36.042
You could do it, Brother!

90
06:36.626 --> 06:37.501
Really?

91
06:38.002 --> 06:39.503
I've gotta get my act together.

92
06:41.547 --> 06:42.423
All right!

93
06:43.299 --> 06:48.012
Two bowls, coming up! Here you go. Thanks as always.

94
06:49.639 --> 06:52.308
We're full right now, so please wait over there.

95
06:52.391 --> 06:54.101
-Orin, one sake, please. -Orin…

96
06:54.602 --> 06:55.519
SWEET SHOP

97
06:55.603 --> 06:56.687
Thank you!

98
06:56.771 --> 06:58.147
Thank you.

99
06:59.899 --> 07:02.318
So this is konpeito.

100
07:02.401 --> 07:03.236
Yeah.

101
07:03.819 --> 07:05.029
Sweet…

102
07:05.112 --> 07:07.114
Don't "Sweet…" me!

103
07:07.198 --> 07:08.866
What the hell are you doing here, Saizo?!

104
07:08.950 --> 07:09.951
LOCAL SPECIALTY KONPEITO

105
07:10.034 --> 07:11.536
You promised, didn't you?

106
07:12.203 --> 07:16.457
If I brought you to Osaka, I'd get three gold coins from old Yukimura.

107
07:16.541 --> 07:18.376
And Yuri and I would have konpeito.

108
07:18.459 --> 07:19.752
I never said just the two of us.

109
07:19.835 --> 07:20.753
Yuri!

110
07:20.836 --> 07:21.712
What a scam…

111
07:22.421 --> 07:23.506
Hey!

112
07:24.382 --> 07:25.424
Konpeito scam!

113
07:25.508 --> 07:27.426
Don't waste your energy shouting.

114
07:28.177 --> 07:32.807
Until Lord Yukimura comes up with a new plan, we need to rest.

115
07:39.814 --> 07:42.650
By the way, have any of you ever seen Lord Hideyori?

116
07:44.026 --> 07:44.902
No.

117
07:45.861 --> 07:47.989
Want me to show you something interesting?

118
07:48.698 --> 07:52.618
So Lady Yodo still won't reconsider…

119
07:54.996 --> 07:56.038
I'm sorry.

120
07:56.622 --> 07:58.916
You have nothing to apologize for, my lord.

121
07:59.000 --> 07:59.834
Anayama!

122
08:00.501 --> 08:04.547
We'll find a way to defeat the Tokugawa while holding out in the castle.

123
08:06.173 --> 08:08.926
I've been thinking all day!

124
08:09.552 --> 08:12.221
What about you, Mochizuki? Where have you been wandering off to?

125
08:14.515 --> 08:16.225
You went to see your daughter, didn't you?

126
08:17.935 --> 08:19.729
You knew?

127
08:20.688 --> 08:23.983
You mean, the one you left behind in Osaka?

128
08:25.318 --> 08:27.486
I couldn't tell her I was her father.

129
08:28.112 --> 08:31.949
If I told her, I'd only cause her trouble.

130
08:32.617 --> 08:35.703
Still… when you know she's right there,

131
08:36.579 --> 08:38.372
you can't help rushing to see her.

132
08:39.290 --> 08:40.333
Yeah.

133
08:42.585 --> 08:44.253
"Can't help rushing to her"?

134
08:48.049 --> 08:48.883
That's it!

135
08:52.094 --> 08:55.556
I've found the secret to defeating the Tokugawa.

136
09:07.360 --> 09:09.070
He's not just similar…

137
09:10.780 --> 09:12.782
He's the spitting image of him.

138
09:12.865 --> 09:16.494
I've come with a new plan.

139
09:17.453 --> 09:19.038
There's no need for a plan.

140
09:19.538 --> 09:21.624
We've already decided to hold out in the castle.

141
09:22.208 --> 09:23.334
Then, Lord Ono,

142
09:24.043 --> 09:26.879
where do you think the Tokugawa army will attack from?

143
09:28.631 --> 09:29.840
Well…

144
09:32.009 --> 09:33.552
If I knew that, I wouldn't be…

145
09:33.636 --> 09:34.470
The south.

146
09:36.806 --> 09:41.227
I'm afraid the southern defenses of Osaka Castle are weak.

147
09:41.894 --> 09:44.563
Are you saying this castle has a weakness?

148
09:44.647 --> 09:46.440
Don't speak carelessly.

149
09:47.775 --> 09:52.738
There's high ground to the south, the coast west, and a river north.

150
09:52.822 --> 09:56.283
If I were Ieyasu, I'd attack from the south.

151
09:56.367 --> 10:01.080
Then we must build a fortified outpost in the southeast to repel the Tokugawa.

152
10:01.163 --> 10:02.039
An outpost?

153
10:03.040 --> 10:06.585
With an outpost, we can delay the enemy and dictate their route.

154
10:07.086 --> 10:09.422
Even if Ieyasu brings a huge army,

155
10:09.505 --> 10:12.133
if he bypasses it, we'll strike from behind.

156
10:12.967 --> 10:17.304
He can't ignore it and will have to send troops there?

157
10:18.347 --> 10:19.265
Exactly.

158
10:19.890 --> 10:21.726
Harunaga, is that true?

159
10:22.560 --> 10:25.312
Lord Sanada's prediction that Ieyasu will attack from the south

160
10:25.396 --> 10:27.440
is just speculation, isn't it?

161
10:28.441 --> 10:31.736
We'll deliberately thin out our troops in the south, except at the outpost.

162
10:32.737 --> 10:36.115
There's no way Ieyasu will overlook that. He'll take the bait.

163
10:37.616 --> 10:41.287
But who will man the outpost?

164
10:42.079 --> 10:45.291
About 200 of the Sanada clan's retainers.

165
10:45.958 --> 10:48.961
We'll station ninja there, too.

166
10:49.962 --> 10:52.590
What can a mere 200 men do?

167
10:53.174 --> 10:55.134
Two hundred elite warriors

168
10:56.302 --> 10:57.845
who drove the Tokugawa back at Ueda.

169
11:01.474 --> 11:03.017
Just as I'd expect from Lord Yukimura.

170
11:04.018 --> 11:06.937
Will you approve the construction of the outpost?

171
11:07.021 --> 11:12.026
I can build a fort that will defeat the Tokugawa.

172
11:12.693 --> 11:13.652
Wait.

173
11:14.653 --> 11:18.824
Can we really trust Lord Sanada's plan?

174
11:20.493 --> 11:21.660
What do you mean?

175
11:22.161 --> 11:24.038
I've heard troubling rumors.

176
11:24.121 --> 11:25.122
LADY OKURAKYO

177
11:25.206 --> 11:28.667
That you sacrificed every villager,

178
11:28.751 --> 11:33.464
women and children included, to save your own skins.

179
11:34.465 --> 11:36.842
What do you mean, Lady Okurakyo?

180
11:36.926 --> 11:38.511
Are you pretending not to know?

181
11:40.221 --> 11:44.725
I heard Kudoyama was burned to the ground, village and all.

182
11:44.808 --> 11:46.018
The whole village?!

183
11:47.645 --> 11:49.605
Hachi! Hachi!

184
11:51.315 --> 11:55.903
Can we really entrust the fate of the Toyotomi

185
11:55.986 --> 11:58.197
to people like that?

186
12:00.616 --> 12:02.159
Is that true?

187
12:04.995 --> 12:06.497
They burned down all of Kudoyama?

188
12:06.580 --> 12:09.875
Who goes there? Do you know where you are?

189
12:09.959 --> 12:13.128
They serve under me. My apologies.

190
12:13.212 --> 12:16.257
Then the Tokugawa did it! Approve the outpost!

191
12:16.340 --> 12:17.508
Silence!

192
12:17.591 --> 12:19.260
Siege or no siege,

193
12:20.010 --> 12:21.178
we'll avenge them!

194
12:21.262 --> 12:23.472
How dare they!

195
12:23.556 --> 12:27.101
Quite the fine ninja you have there.

196
12:27.643 --> 12:28.936
The outpost is forbidden!

197
12:30.020 --> 12:31.146
It'll only cause chaos.

198
12:35.067 --> 12:36.068
What the hell?!

199
12:38.070 --> 12:39.446
You stupid monkey!

200
12:39.530 --> 12:40.489
Ouch.

201
12:40.573 --> 12:42.241
Hey, I'm bleeding!

202
12:42.324 --> 12:45.786
For once, stop acting before you think!

203
12:51.041 --> 12:52.835
How can you all be so calm about this?

204
12:57.548 --> 13:00.092
The villagers did everything they could to save us.

205
13:01.093 --> 13:02.219
And yet…

206
13:03.846 --> 13:04.888
How could I be calm?

207
13:07.600 --> 13:08.809
The Tokugawa's ninja…

208
13:10.102 --> 13:11.979
and Hattori Hanzo have taken

209
13:13.272 --> 13:15.482
precious things from me before.

210
13:19.361 --> 13:21.113
My name, Kamanosuke,

211
13:22.239 --> 13:24.867
was passed down from my father, whom Hattori Hanzo killed.

212
13:29.955 --> 13:31.040
Here. You two.

213
13:32.791 --> 13:33.792
Sanada cord?

214
13:34.627 --> 13:37.004
Now's no time for us to fight amongst ourselves.

215
13:42.801 --> 13:43.677
You're right.

216
13:44.720 --> 13:48.557
This cord is proof of our bond.

217
13:52.311 --> 13:53.812
Awful.

218
13:54.647 --> 13:55.856
Your blood tastes awful.

219
13:57.900 --> 13:58.901
Sasuke.

220
14:00.444 --> 14:01.987
Let's take down the Tokugawa together.

221
14:06.116 --> 14:06.950
You bet.

222
14:18.962 --> 14:20.255
Saizo, you've changed.

223
14:23.133 --> 14:26.261
I've never heard you use the word "bond" before.

224
14:31.100 --> 14:34.603
Yuri, what will you do when this war is over?

225
14:39.316 --> 14:40.401
What about you, Saizo?

226
14:41.735 --> 14:42.736
I…

227
14:47.700 --> 14:48.534
No.

228
14:49.952 --> 14:52.496
For now, let's focus on defeating the Tokugawa.

229
14:55.499 --> 14:56.333
Yeah.

230
15:11.181 --> 15:13.017
All our men are assembled, then.

231
15:13.100 --> 15:17.021
With Lord Hidetada's arrival, our position is secure.

232
15:18.522 --> 15:21.400
When I heard Sanada had entered Osaka, I trembled.

233
15:22.568 --> 15:24.069
I've never forgotten

234
15:25.112 --> 15:27.031
the humiliation I suffered at Ueda.

235
15:27.865 --> 15:30.534
Osaka seems intent on holding out in the castle,

236
15:31.285 --> 15:32.661
with no reinforcements coming.

237
15:33.954 --> 15:34.913
Foolish…

238
15:35.664 --> 15:38.792
A woman who knows nothing of war holds the real power.

239
15:39.626 --> 15:41.420
Our victory is assured.

240
15:43.047 --> 15:45.883
At last, I'll take Sanada's head with my own hands.

241
15:46.717 --> 15:47.718
Hidetada.

242
15:48.427 --> 15:50.846
Give Sanada hell.

243
15:50.929 --> 15:51.764
Yes, my lord!

244
15:52.848 --> 15:55.434
I have one concern.

245
15:56.477 --> 15:57.811
Speak, Hanzo.

246
15:58.395 --> 16:03.025
Even in this unfavorable position, Sanada will devise some scheme.

247
16:03.817 --> 16:06.403
To be safe, I suggest sending my ninja--

248
16:06.487 --> 16:07.488
There's no need.

249
16:08.155 --> 16:10.032
I've already dispatched Lady Imbeyama.

250
16:10.824 --> 16:12.367
Lady Imbeyama?

251
16:12.951 --> 16:14.703
Your worries are unfounded.

252
16:15.412 --> 16:17.206
Whatever scheme Sanada devises…

253
16:19.208 --> 16:20.167
Bring it in.

254
16:20.959 --> 16:21.877
Yes, my lord.

255
16:23.420 --> 16:27.049
Suden, the item you requested has arrived.

256
16:27.132 --> 16:30.052
It's what the Ogosho requested.

257
16:42.981 --> 16:44.233
This is it…

258
16:45.692 --> 16:48.153
Well done, Hidetada!

259
16:48.821 --> 16:53.200
This monstrous being could serve as the raw material for the ultimate ninja.

260
16:53.951 --> 16:55.285
Once it awakens,

261
16:55.953 --> 17:00.374
the Tokugawa will wield power equal to a million-man army.

262
17:00.457 --> 17:01.416
MAGAMARU

263
17:01.500 --> 17:03.919
Hanzo, any other concerns?

264
17:07.965 --> 17:09.133
None, my lord.

265
17:09.216 --> 17:10.175
Good.

266
17:16.223 --> 17:18.058
Sanada has made no notable moves.

267
17:19.226 --> 17:21.270
The Tokugawa are truly unassailable.

268
17:22.104 --> 17:23.105
But…

269
17:24.189 --> 17:26.775
there's one more thing that concerns me.

270
17:30.154 --> 17:31.822
That monkey who got away…

271
17:33.031 --> 17:35.075
You mean Sasuke?

272
17:36.493 --> 17:39.872
You seemed to be close to him in Kudoyama.

273
17:40.581 --> 17:41.415
Yes.

274
17:41.915 --> 17:43.500
Then kill him.

275
17:44.710 --> 17:45.836
With your own hands.

276
17:47.129 --> 17:48.130
Understood?

277
17:49.047 --> 17:49.882
Yes, my lord.

278
17:55.846 --> 17:57.890
What are you doing out here so late at night?

279
17:57.973 --> 17:59.558
Training for the coming battle.

280
18:01.643 --> 18:02.936
Let's do it again.

281
18:08.775 --> 18:09.818
Spe-cial?

282
18:11.862 --> 18:15.073
It means "special" in my native tongue.

283
18:16.950 --> 18:18.994
The two of them took quite a liking to it.

284
18:19.077 --> 18:21.538
I'll kick the soldier high into the air.

285
18:21.622 --> 18:23.123
As they go flying…

286
18:23.207 --> 18:25.292
I'll finish them off with shuriken.

287
18:25.375 --> 18:28.754
Don't finish him off! That makes me sound like your assistant.

288
18:28.837 --> 18:31.632
-Leave him alive for a bit. -Don't make it so complicated.

289
18:31.715 --> 18:33.300
-It's not complicated. -Sasuke.

290
18:33.884 --> 18:34.801
Saizo.

291
18:35.385 --> 18:36.595
You fools!

292
18:38.055 --> 18:40.557
I hear you barged into the war council.

293
18:41.266 --> 18:43.268
You disgraced our lord!

294
18:44.353 --> 18:47.147
-We have no excuse. -You needn't worry.

295
18:47.231 --> 18:49.316
Our lord is already taking action.

296
18:50.776 --> 18:54.404
He'll make Lady Yodo approve the outpost.

297
19:02.788 --> 19:05.207
Thank you for taking the trouble,

298
19:05.874 --> 19:07.209
Lady Okurakyo.

299
19:15.592 --> 19:19.221
One never knows who's listening within the castle.

300
19:20.597 --> 19:21.848
You wish to obtain

301
19:22.557 --> 19:25.894
Lady Yodo's approval for the outpost, don't you?

302
19:26.603 --> 19:28.480
I'm glad we're on the same page.

303
19:28.563 --> 19:29.648
Indeed.

304
19:30.524 --> 19:33.527
As the one closest to Lady Yodo,

305
19:34.319 --> 19:37.698
I may sway her if I speak on your behalf.

306
19:38.699 --> 19:39.616
But…

307
19:40.242 --> 19:43.829
I have no reason to help you, Lord Sanada--

308
19:43.912 --> 19:45.205
No reason at all?

309
19:47.124 --> 19:51.295
You, who secretly sell the treasures left by the Taiko to merchants

310
19:52.045 --> 19:54.339
to line your own pockets?

311
19:54.423 --> 19:55.757
What are you accusing me of?

312
19:55.841 --> 19:59.553
Our ninja have already searched beneath the floor of your chambers.

313
20:09.938 --> 20:12.733
Imagine what would happen if word got out in the castle.

314
20:16.653 --> 20:18.488
Let us make a deal.

315
20:22.909 --> 20:25.454
Damn that Sanada…

316
20:30.334 --> 20:31.501
What are you doing?!

317
20:39.426 --> 20:40.510
This is…

318
20:47.642 --> 20:49.603
Are you hurt?

319
20:54.191 --> 20:56.818
LADY IMBEYAMA

320
21:12.918 --> 21:14.211
Lady Yodo,

321
21:14.294 --> 21:18.465
I once again ask your permission

322
21:19.174 --> 21:20.842
to build an outpost south of the castle.

323
21:22.094 --> 21:23.261
What?

324
21:23.345 --> 21:28.141
Not one of us supports this plan.

325
21:33.355 --> 21:36.316
Is that truly so, Lady Okurakyo?

326
21:37.317 --> 21:38.360
What do you say?

327
21:42.155 --> 21:43.073
I…

328
22:08.390 --> 22:11.143
believe we should not build the outpost.

329
22:13.228 --> 22:18.692
Last night, this man used his ninja to spy on the castle.

330
22:18.775 --> 22:19.651
Please, wait!

331
22:19.734 --> 22:22.487
What's more, I hear he bought his escape from Kudoyama

332
22:23.196 --> 22:25.699
by sacrificing the villagers

333
22:26.283 --> 22:28.160
to the Tokugawa.

334
22:29.244 --> 22:30.829
That can't possibly be true!

335
22:30.912 --> 22:32.831
Do not listen to him!

336
22:33.415 --> 22:35.458
He may have defected to the Tokugawa.

337
22:37.544 --> 22:38.545
This man…

338
22:39.212 --> 22:41.506
is a demon who will lead

339
22:41.590 --> 22:43.258
the Toyotomi to ruin!

340
22:55.729 --> 22:57.564
Lady Okurakyo! Help!

341
22:59.274 --> 23:00.275
Lady Okurakyo!

342
23:00.859 --> 23:02.068
What's wrong?!

343
23:03.069 --> 23:07.240
Is it true you sent your ninja to investigate the castle?

344
23:09.201 --> 23:10.035
Yes.

345
23:29.471 --> 23:30.305
I've had it!

346
23:31.514 --> 23:32.682
I'm done with this!

347
23:34.351 --> 23:36.436
We can't attack or build the outpost.

348
23:36.519 --> 23:38.355
How the hell are we supposed to win like this?

349
23:39.231 --> 23:41.775
Sasuke, calm down!

350
23:41.858 --> 23:44.361
I came all this way to take down Ieyasu.

351
23:44.444 --> 23:46.571
I didn't come all this way to fight a losing battle.

352
23:46.655 --> 23:48.990
But the Toyotomi have made their decision.

353
23:50.533 --> 23:52.244
Then this is where I leave.

354
23:54.913 --> 23:57.332
We agreed I'd only come as far as Osaka, remember?

355
23:58.041 --> 24:00.043
I'll take Hanzo and Ieyasu's heads myself.

356
24:00.126 --> 24:02.754
-Don't be ridiculous. -Give it back.

357
24:02.837 --> 24:04.923
I'll come up with a good plan, I promise!

358
24:05.632 --> 24:09.469
What's the point of thinking up plans if we can't convince Lady Yodo?

359
24:10.553 --> 24:13.348
I'm frustrated too!

360
24:13.431 --> 24:16.476
But we have to keep thinking, no matter what!

361
24:20.272 --> 24:21.856
What can you do on your own?

362
24:22.607 --> 24:23.817
Just hang in there for now.

363
24:27.570 --> 24:28.488
Shut up.

364
24:29.281 --> 24:30.532
Don't order me around.

365
24:30.615 --> 24:31.700
Stop, both of you.

366
24:36.246 --> 24:39.040
I was a fool to put any faith in you.

367
24:40.667 --> 24:42.502
Don't ever show your face again.

368
24:59.728 --> 25:01.646
Shouldn't we stop him?

369
25:11.531 --> 25:14.492
Sasuke! I really want to get stronger!

370
25:15.076 --> 25:17.203
-That's why I want to learn more-- -If you're serious…

371
25:19.414 --> 25:21.082
stop relying on others.

372
25:24.919 --> 25:26.880
Figure it out on your own.

373
25:44.105 --> 25:48.109
Lady Okurakyo has been bedridden ever since.

374
25:48.943 --> 25:50.028
I see…

375
25:51.446 --> 25:53.448
Is this as far as we can go?

376
25:58.953 --> 25:59.871
Everyone…

377
26:01.831 --> 26:02.874
can I have a moment?

378
26:09.464 --> 26:12.133
Hey, where do I go to find Ieyasu?

379
26:12.217 --> 26:13.635
What are you talking about?

380
26:16.221 --> 26:19.599
Hey, hey! Where can I find Ieyasu?

381
26:19.682 --> 26:21.393
Don't get involved.

382
26:21.476 --> 26:22.685
Who is he? Who?

383
26:26.356 --> 26:29.192
I'm starving…

384
26:57.512 --> 26:58.346
Here.

385
26:59.472 --> 27:00.432
Eat up.

386
27:04.853 --> 27:05.687
Is it good?

387
27:08.398 --> 27:10.483
Hey! That's ours!

388
27:11.317 --> 27:13.278
Fine! I'll pay, all right?

389
27:14.070 --> 27:16.906
Old Yukimura promised me a hefty reward…

390
27:21.494 --> 27:22.412
I don't have it on me.

391
27:23.955 --> 27:25.373
Damn it.

392
27:26.040 --> 27:27.625
I left it at the castle!

393
27:27.709 --> 27:30.795
You thief! Just come with us! You too!

394
27:30.879 --> 27:32.630
-The kid's not involved! -Shut up!

395
27:32.714 --> 27:33.882
I'll pay for it!

396
27:34.382 --> 27:35.550
Okuni?

397
27:36.634 --> 27:38.511
It's been a while, Sasuke.

398
27:41.181 --> 27:42.640
You're going after Ieyasu alone?

399
27:42.724 --> 27:43.558
Yeah.

400
27:44.142 --> 27:46.311
Isn't that far too reckless?

401
27:47.145 --> 27:48.646
That's what they said, too.

402
27:49.689 --> 27:52.066
But they just can't do anything alone.

403
27:52.734 --> 27:55.403
Maybe that's true for someone like you, Sasuke.

404
27:57.280 --> 27:59.741
I heard what happened at Kudoyama.

405
28:00.909 --> 28:03.286
I'm just glad you survived, at least.

406
28:04.412 --> 28:07.499
But how am I supposed to live on my own now?

407
28:08.625 --> 28:09.459
That's…

408
28:09.542 --> 28:13.421
Not everyone is as strong as you, Sasuke.

409
28:17.842 --> 28:19.969
Maybe I went a little too far.

410
28:20.470 --> 28:21.513
What?

411
28:21.596 --> 28:23.848
I mean…

412
28:26.059 --> 28:27.685
how you live your life…

413
28:28.478 --> 28:30.563
That's not for someone else to decide, right?

414
28:33.650 --> 28:35.693
LOCAL SPECIALTY DANGO

415
28:35.777 --> 28:38.279
-Where are you going? -There's somewhere I need to stop first.

416
28:39.239 --> 28:41.491
Besides, Ieyasu will be coming this way anyway, right?

417
28:42.200 --> 28:44.410
I'll lie low around here for a while.

418
28:46.704 --> 28:47.997
Do you have somewhere to stay?

419
28:49.707 --> 28:51.000
A place to stay…

420
28:52.544 --> 28:56.923
If you don't, why not stay at my inn?

421
29:06.683 --> 29:09.519
What brings you here at this hour, Hideyori?

422
29:10.520 --> 29:12.021
As Lord Sanada said,

423
29:13.189 --> 29:16.067
we should build an outpost south of the castle.

424
29:16.734 --> 29:17.735
What?!

425
29:18.444 --> 29:19.404
That's our

426
29:20.738 --> 29:24.242
one-in-a-million shot at winning this war.

427
29:28.955 --> 29:31.749
Pretend to be Lord Hideyori?!

428
29:32.458 --> 29:36.838
I've studied his mannerisms, and we look exactly alike.

429
29:37.714 --> 29:41.759
If I speak as Lord Hideyori, I should be able to sway Lady Yodo.

430
29:42.468 --> 29:46.306
Could such a thing really work?

431
29:47.223 --> 29:48.141
All right!

432
29:49.183 --> 29:50.393
-Let's do it! -Yeah.

433
29:51.394 --> 29:52.478
Shakespeare said,

434
29:53.313 --> 29:56.774
"Then I defy you, stars!"

435
29:57.901 --> 30:00.528
We'll strike at the Hour of the Boar, while Lord Hideyori sleeps.

436
30:01.404 --> 30:05.533
Everyone, keep watch in case Lord Hideyori wakes up.

437
30:11.789 --> 30:14.167
There's no sign of Lord Hideyori waking up.

438
30:14.250 --> 30:15.710
What a relief.

439
30:18.004 --> 30:19.255
Kakei, what's wrong?

440
30:21.925 --> 30:26.095
This plan was Lord Yukimura's idea, right?

441
30:26.930 --> 30:30.516
No one but Lord Yukimura could come up with such a bold plan.

442
30:31.476 --> 30:34.062
Then why keep it secret from everyone else?

443
30:35.521 --> 30:38.816
Saizo and Yuri would be better suited to keep watch.

444
30:40.693 --> 30:43.029
I guess he trusts us.

445
30:43.821 --> 30:48.409
But what happens if this plan fails?

446
30:48.493 --> 30:49.827
That's obvious.

447
30:50.328 --> 30:52.455
We're impersonating Lord Hideyori.

448
30:53.206 --> 30:54.874
If we fail…

449
30:55.667 --> 30:57.543
we'll all be beheaded.

450
30:59.420 --> 31:00.380
Beheaded?

451
31:01.172 --> 31:05.259
What's wrong, Hideyori? You seem like a completely different person.

452
31:06.260 --> 31:08.137
I'm no longer a child.

453
31:09.973 --> 31:11.724
Shouldn't we trust Lord Sanada's plan?

454
31:12.517 --> 31:14.435
He's given the Tokugawa trouble twice,

455
31:14.519 --> 31:16.980
unlike us, who know so little of war.

456
31:22.777 --> 31:27.532
So you've grown into a fine lord without me realizing it.

457
31:30.326 --> 31:32.370
I understand your feelings.

458
31:36.833 --> 31:37.667
Then…

459
31:40.878 --> 31:41.879
However…

460
31:42.922 --> 31:46.050
such an important decision cannot be made at once.

461
31:47.051 --> 31:48.011
What?

462
31:48.094 --> 31:51.389
Tomorrow, we'll discuss it again with the retainers.

463
31:51.472 --> 31:52.765
No!

464
31:52.849 --> 31:54.517
You must decide right here, right now!

465
31:54.600 --> 31:56.644
Why are you in such a hurry?

466
31:58.062 --> 31:58.938
That's because…

467
31:59.605 --> 32:02.275
Hey, what are you doing here?

468
32:03.317 --> 32:04.318
You…!

469
32:05.111 --> 32:07.530
You insolent wretch! Get out of here at once!

470
32:07.613 --> 32:09.699
I hate being ordered around.

471
32:10.408 --> 32:11.868
It's not my problem anymore.

472
32:14.829 --> 32:16.456
Yeah, you're Daisuke.

473
32:16.998 --> 32:17.999
Daisuke?

474
32:18.082 --> 32:19.250
No, that's…

475
32:19.876 --> 32:23.796
Sorry about earlier, telling you to handle things yourself and all.

476
32:23.880 --> 32:26.632
Not everyone has to make it on their own.

477
32:26.716 --> 32:28.968
-What are you talking about? -Shut it, old hag.

478
32:29.052 --> 32:29.969
Old hag?!

479
32:30.553 --> 32:31.679
What I meant was,

480
32:32.388 --> 32:34.515
you should decide how you want to live for yourself.

481
32:35.975 --> 32:37.477
-Is something the matter? -Crap!

482
32:38.352 --> 32:39.187
Well, I'm off.

483
32:39.812 --> 32:42.273
I just stopped by while collecting my reward.

484
32:52.867 --> 32:53.701
Is Hideyori here?

485
32:54.619 --> 32:57.830
See? There's no one here. I'm Hideyori.

486
32:57.914 --> 32:59.624
Let's hurry back to your room, Mother…

487
32:59.707 --> 33:01.959
Hideyori! If you're here, answer me!

488
33:08.424 --> 33:09.425
Mother…

489
33:13.137 --> 33:14.222
Who are you?!

490
33:14.305 --> 33:15.306
Hideyori!

491
33:17.475 --> 33:19.977
No doubt about it. That mole! It's Hideyori!

492
33:22.271 --> 33:23.731
You're ninja, aren't you?

493
33:24.732 --> 33:27.485
Yukimura put you up to this, didn't he?

494
33:27.568 --> 33:29.195
No! I did this on my own.

495
33:29.278 --> 33:30.321
Guards! Guards!

496
33:31.280 --> 33:34.534
There's an intruder! Seize him! Guards! Guards!

497
33:35.159 --> 33:36.202
You fools!

498
33:36.786 --> 33:39.372
I can't believe you impersonated Lord Hideyori…

499
33:40.581 --> 33:41.916
My apologies!

500
33:42.667 --> 33:44.627
And why didn't the rest of you stop him?

501
33:46.087 --> 33:48.339
What happened to that insolent ninja?

502
33:48.422 --> 33:49.257
You mean Sasuke?

503
33:50.466 --> 33:51.592
Tomorrow,

504
33:52.385 --> 33:54.887
judgment will be passed on everyone involved in this.

505
33:55.805 --> 33:56.722
Well…

506
33:58.516 --> 34:01.435
I'm sure it'll mean beheading.

507
34:04.230 --> 34:05.898
Bring that monkey here, too.

508
34:06.983 --> 34:08.067
Don't try to escape.

509
34:14.949 --> 34:16.576
I'll bring Sasuke back.

510
34:16.659 --> 34:17.577
That's unnecessary.

511
34:18.327 --> 34:22.999
It's my duty to take responsibility for my retainers' failures.

512
34:24.125 --> 34:25.001
My lord!

513
34:45.605 --> 34:46.606
I'm coming, too.

514
34:57.825 --> 34:58.951
Sasuke?

515
35:09.128 --> 35:10.963
You're surprisingly naive.

516
35:28.981 --> 35:30.942
What the hell are these guys? Stay back!

517
35:43.913 --> 35:45.665
Not bad.

518
35:48.042 --> 35:49.126
But…

519
35:49.210 --> 35:52.004
if this is giving you trouble,

520
35:52.088 --> 35:54.757
you'll never take the Ogosho's head.

521
36:01.931 --> 36:03.140
Sasuke…

522
36:15.653 --> 36:16.862
Enchain.

523
36:22.535 --> 36:24.620
Ninja are despised

524
36:26.080 --> 36:29.000
and used as pawns by the Toyotomi, only to die in the end.

525
36:29.959 --> 36:32.128
That's your fate.

526
36:34.922 --> 36:36.048
Do it.

527
36:37.133 --> 36:38.509
Join the Tokugawa.

528
36:48.644 --> 36:49.562
Stay away from Saizo!

529
36:50.604 --> 36:52.857
Do you really think you can protect him like this?

530
37:00.948 --> 37:01.949
Are you all right?

531
37:06.996 --> 37:07.913
Saizo?

532
37:12.418 --> 37:14.253
Would my head not suffice?

533
37:14.337 --> 37:15.212
Enough!

534
37:29.310 --> 37:30.394
Father!

535
37:34.065 --> 37:35.149
Can I speak with you?

536
37:36.525 --> 37:38.486
You needn't be so formal.

537
37:39.653 --> 37:40.654
But…

538
37:42.448 --> 37:46.577
I just wanted to talk to you.

539
37:48.913 --> 37:50.956
You, who bears the same face as me…

540
37:55.002 --> 37:56.545
the son of Yukimura.

541
37:57.838 --> 37:58.798
Why…

542
38:00.132 --> 38:02.218
do we look so much alike?

543
38:03.928 --> 38:04.970
That's…

544
38:06.680 --> 38:07.807
Well, never mind that.

545
38:10.142 --> 38:14.146
Still, you've certainly caused quite a stir.

546
38:16.065 --> 38:19.318
This whole affair was my doing.

547
38:20.694 --> 38:22.321
Please, let me bear the blame alone!

548
38:25.074 --> 38:26.700
Do you not fear death?

549
38:29.245 --> 38:30.830
I wish to decide how I live…

550
38:33.958 --> 38:35.584
for myself.

551
38:39.171 --> 38:40.673
I'd rather die with pride…

552
38:42.967 --> 38:46.095
as Sanada Yukimura's son

553
38:48.013 --> 38:49.473
than live on like this.

554
38:58.858 --> 39:00.776
After causing such a commotion,

555
39:02.236 --> 39:04.113
don't you think it's too convenient

556
39:05.156 --> 39:06.866
to punish only you?

557
39:06.949 --> 39:07.992
Even so…

558
39:08.659 --> 39:10.494
My father and his men…

559
39:12.621 --> 39:13.998
will surely be

560
39:15.291 --> 39:16.959
an asset to the Toyotomi.

561
39:17.042 --> 39:20.963
I doubt that insolent ninja who barged into the war council will be of any use.

562
39:29.180 --> 39:30.431
One last question.

563
39:33.559 --> 39:34.935
What kind of man…

564
39:37.146 --> 39:38.355
is Sanada Yukimura?

565
39:47.990 --> 39:49.283
Had times been different…

566
39:52.161 --> 39:53.829
he would have ruled the realm.

567
39:56.540 --> 39:57.875
Though I share his blood…

568
40:00.085 --> 40:01.712
I'm nowhere near his equal.

569
40:04.798 --> 40:05.883
And there are things…

570
40:07.968 --> 40:09.803
even Lord Hideyori cannot do…

571
40:13.098 --> 40:14.308
that he can.

572
40:21.732 --> 40:22.650
Enough.

573
40:24.318 --> 40:25.277
You may leave.

574
40:27.029 --> 40:27.905
Yes, my lord!

575
41:10.864 --> 41:12.449
To think…

576
41:13.617 --> 41:15.953
you'd scheme against Lady Yodo…

577
41:17.413 --> 41:19.957
You're prepared to face the consequences, I trust?

578
41:21.000 --> 41:26.046
A ninja commander of your caliber is too valuable to lose, Lord Sanada.

579
41:26.755 --> 41:29.091
But it can't be helped.

580
41:30.509 --> 41:34.388
Lord Hideyori and Lady Yodo are here!

581
41:52.865 --> 41:54.867
Regarding the punishment of Lord Sanada…

582
41:56.744 --> 41:59.496
and his retainers for yesterday's incident…

583
42:01.915 --> 42:03.000
as for his retainers,

584
42:04.335 --> 42:05.836
all offenses…

585
42:08.380 --> 42:09.715
shall be overlooked.

586
42:13.761 --> 42:17.598
A lord should bear responsibility for his retainers' failures.

587
42:20.684 --> 42:22.102
Sanada Yukimura.

588
42:22.686 --> 42:23.520
Yes!

589
42:25.064 --> 42:27.274
I'm prepared.

590
42:27.941 --> 42:29.693
Before I pass judgment,

591
42:30.277 --> 42:34.657
tell me once more what you think of our strategy for defending the castle.

592
42:37.159 --> 42:38.786
If you support our plan

593
42:39.703 --> 42:41.538
and continue to serve us,

594
42:42.414 --> 42:43.832
I'll overlook this incident.

595
42:45.250 --> 42:46.168
But if you refuse,

596
42:47.336 --> 42:49.463
I'll have no choice but to regard it as treason.

597
42:51.173 --> 42:55.260
Do we stand any chance of winning if we continue to hold out in the castle?

598
42:59.807 --> 43:00.849
None.

599
43:03.477 --> 43:04.311
I see.

600
43:05.604 --> 43:08.065
Then I shall pass judgment.

601
43:11.443 --> 43:12.403
Sanada.

602
43:13.112 --> 43:13.987
Yes.

603
43:16.198 --> 43:18.117
Build an outpost to the southeast.

604
43:22.746 --> 43:24.289
You will be responsible

605
43:25.791 --> 43:27.292
for driving back the Tokugawa.

606
43:27.793 --> 43:30.045
Hideyori! What are you saying?

607
43:30.129 --> 43:33.632
We can't win this war by meeting them head-on.

608
43:34.508 --> 43:37.845
We need people like them, who aren't bound by convention.

609
43:37.928 --> 43:41.014
But after what they did to you yesterday…

610
43:42.433 --> 43:43.600
Another impostor…?

611
43:44.393 --> 43:46.603
-Hideyori should have a mole there-- -I do have a mole.

612
43:49.064 --> 43:51.775
Stop treating me like a child!

613
43:52.943 --> 43:54.737
I am the head of the Toyotomi clan!

614
43:55.320 --> 43:57.865
And I say that I trust them

615
43:58.657 --> 44:00.743
and approve the construction of the outpost.

616
44:06.790 --> 44:08.292
I'll decide how I live…

617
44:09.918 --> 44:11.044
for myself.

618
44:17.092 --> 44:19.386
What kind of trick did you pull?

619
44:20.679 --> 44:21.847
A report!

620
44:24.141 --> 44:25.225
I bring urgent news!

621
44:25.309 --> 44:27.311
The Tokugawa forces have

622
44:27.394 --> 44:30.230
begun marching from Nijo Castle in Kyoto toward Osaka!

623
44:30.898 --> 44:31.899
Excuse me!

624
44:41.074 --> 44:41.992
Mother…

625
44:44.119 --> 44:45.579
we must prepare ourselves.

626
44:56.381 --> 44:57.216
Yukimura!

627
44:58.717 --> 44:59.551
Yes!

628
45:01.136 --> 45:02.137
Don't fail us.

629
45:03.555 --> 45:04.973
